<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#Particular> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#Particular> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Particular" .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalDisposition> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "any kind of disposition considered non-canonical. The criteria of canonicity are not further specified. \nThe classification of certain dispositions as dysfunctional or pathological is dependent on a historic and cultural context. Dysfunction or disease therefore hasn't the status of a universal." .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalDisposition> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "review target in BIOTOP from disease_terms_review_enriched.csv" .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pathological disposition" .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#Disposition> .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalProcess> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "a biological process which is non-canonic" .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalProcess> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "review target in BIOTOP from disease_terms_review_enriched.csv" .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalProcess> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/biotop/biotop.owl#PathologicalProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pathological process" .
